<title>JAPAN: Aoki sells overseas assets to reduce debt.</title>
<headline>Aoki sells overseas assets to reduce debt.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aoki Corp said on Friday it had sold some  of its overseas assets to reduce its group debt.</p>
<p>Aoki, a general contractor, said the money from the sale would help  reduce its group debt by 18.2 billion yen.  </p>
<p>Loans that Aoki guaranteed for other companies will also fall by 5.7  billion yen, Aoki said.</p>
<p>The properties Aoki sold were a condominium in California and a hotel  in Germany, Aoki said.</p>
<p>Aoki said it had sold assets and operation rights of the condominium  in San Diego to Irvine Apartment Communities Inc for about 14.5 billion  yen.</p>
<p>It said it sold assets and operating rights of Hotel Vier Jahreszeiten  in Hamburg for 5.1 billion yen to Raffles Holdings, a unit of DBS  Land Ltd of Singapore.</p>
</text>
